@voice saruth
// Writer (command: guests). Envoy Saruth (they/them), the Veyli Envoy, guest of the Concord. Cabin 2-E, Deck 2, next door
// to Holt's. Knot cord on the door handle: visitors by invitation only; a new knot each month aboard. Takes tea kneeling
// at a low table at the same hour every day. Tends Veyli seedlings in a corner of the garden (habit shift).
//
// HOW THEY TALK: formal and exact, no contractions, unhurried. Long pauses; silence is a kind of answer. Speaks of
// "your people" and "my people" without heat. Notices small courtesies and names them ("You held the door. Thank you.").
// Dry, very slowly: the joke arrives a sentence late, and they watch to see if you caught it.
// WITH JUNIORS: courteous, curious, a little formal; asks about human customs (why you knock twice, why "cheers").
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: courtesy, ritual, hands, who greets whom first, the garden's seedlings.
// MOOD TELLS: content = invites you to tea. Weary = more formal still. Amused = a long silence, then one dry line.
// NEVER: raises their voice; speaks ill of Holt (they find him "honest, which is rarer than kindness"); explains Veyli
// ritual fully (some things are kept); uses a nickname for you before close.
// RUNNING: the knot cord on the door; tea at the same hour; finds humans exhausting and very kind, often at once (tier 3,
// canon); Ferreira's Veyli, which Saruth corrects gently.
tpl: steady
talk: Formal and exact, no contractions; long pauses; names small courtesies; a dry joke that arrives a sentence late.
cares: courtesy | tea at the proper hour | the Veyli seedlings in the garden | the posting working
jokes: the knot cord on the door, and who is invited | Ferreira's Veyli, corrected gently | humans are exhausting and very kind, often at once
hi: Greetings | Good day | Ah. You
bye: Go well | Until the next hour | Be well
yes: Yes | That is acceptable | Gladly
thanks: Thank you | That was courteous
wow: That is remarkable
sigh: Ah
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: tea | plant
likes: garden | book
invites: tasting | garden
joy: tea at the proper hour
thread: startover
keepsake: a length of Veyli cord with one knot, tied for you
avoid: why they were sent (until close) | Veyli rites in full
